B.agB=s([0.01932141,0.11916382,0.95034478],t.n)
B.hy=s([B.abR,B.a9G,B.agB],t.zg)
B.ab0=s(['Pick one marker and stick with it \u2014 a clicker, or a short word like "yes." Always follow it with a treat.',"Mark the instant the good thing happens, then reach for the treat \u2014 not before.","Keep treats off your body when you can (a bowl on the counter) so your dog works for the marker, not your hand."],t.s)
B.adR=s(["Say your marker, then give a treat. Repeat until your dog perks up at the sound \u2014 usually 10\u201320 times.","Mix up how the treat arrives \u2014 from your hand, or tossed on the floor \u2014 so the marker stays the exciting part.","Now you can mark any small win in the skills below."],t.s)
B.a0w=new A.kE("marker","Marker / clicker",'A click or a word like "yes" tells your dog the exact moment they got it right \u2014 and that a treat is on the way.',B.ab0,B.adR,!0)
B.abY=s(['Say it in a bright, easy tone. Their name should feel like "want to go for a walk?", never a telling-off.',"Say it when you can already tell they'll look \u2014 not when they're locked onto something else.","Start somewhere boring; add distractions slowly."],t.s)
B.abs=s(["In a quiet room, say their name in a happy voice. The moment they look, mark and treat.","Once that's easy, wait a beat longer each time before you mark \u2014 a second, then two.","Try it in slightly busier spots: the yard, the porch, a quiet sidewalk."],t.s)
B.a0x=new A.kE("name","Name & attention","Your dog hears their name and looks to you \u2014 happily, like you're about to say something great.",B.abY,B.abs,!1)
B.a7a=s(["Go slow and pair every touch with a treat. If they pull away, you moved too fast \u2014 back up a step.","Keep sessions short and end while they're still happy.","A little every day adds up faster than one long session."],t.s)
B.aaL=s(["Touch a paw for a second, mark, treat. Do the same with an ear, the collar, along the back.","Slowly hold each touch a little longer, still treating.","Work up to gently holding a paw, looking in an ear, or wiping a foot \u2014 always ending on a good note."],t.s)
B.a0C=new A.kE("handling","Handling & gentleness","Your dog stays relaxed while you touch paws, ears, and collar \u2014 so vet visits and nail trims aren't a battle.",B.a7a,B.aaL,!1)
B.afW=s(["Feed meals and give chews in there so it becomes the best spot in the house.","Never use it as a time-out. Calm goes in, calm comes out.","Let them choose it \u2014 toss a treat in and let them wander in on their own."],t.s)
B.aba=s(["Toss a treat inside; let your dog walk in and out freely. Mark and treat any time they go in.","Feed a meal or give a chew in there with the door open.","Close the door for a few seconds while they're busy, then open it. Build the time up slowly and calmly."],t.s)
B.a0B=new A.kE("crate-settle","Crate & settle","Your dog learns the crate (or a mat) is a calm, good place to rest \u2014 never a punishment.",B.afW,B.aba,!1)
B.a6O=s([B.a0w,B.a0x,B.a0C,B.a0B],t.mJ)
B.a0o=new A.I2("Foundations",B.a6O)
B.adN=s(["Lure with food only at first, then drop the lure fast so they're not holding out for a bribe.",'Say "sit" once. If nothing happens, help them into it and try again \u2014 don\'t repeat the word over and over.',"Never push their rear down."],t.s)
B.adM=s(["Hold a treat at their nose and slowly lift it back over their head. As their bottom hits the floor, mark and treat.","Do the same hand motion with no food in that hand, then treat from the other hand.",'Add the word "sit" just before the motion. Practice in every room, the yard, and on walks.'],t.s)
B.a0u=new A.kE("sit","Sit",'You say "sit" and your dog sits \u2014 no treat waved in front of them needed.',B.adN,B.adM,!1)
B.afH=s(["Start somewhere calm \u2014 lying down is a vulnerable position, so distractions make it harder.","Lure slowly and steadily; let them nibble the treat as they follow it to the floor.","If they pop back up, no problem \u2014 just try the previous step again."],t.s)
B.aaW=s(["With your dog sitting, hold a treat at their nose and lower it straight to the floor between their paws. As they lie down, mark and treat.","Once that's smooth, try the same motion with an empty hand, treating from the other.",'Add the word "down," then practice in new spots \u2014 a little harder each time.'],t.s)
B.a0v=new A.kE("down","Down",'On the word "down," your dog lies down and stays settled.',B.afH,B.aaW,!1)
B.abU=s(["Reward the spot right beside you often, especially early \u2014 that's where the good stuff happens.","When the leash goes tight, stop. Walking only continues when it's loose again.","Short, frequent practice beats one long, frustrating walk."],t.s)
B.aaM=s(["In a quiet spot, treat your dog whenever they're near your side.","Start walking. Every few steps they spend at your side, mark and treat.","If they forge ahead and the leash tightens, stop still. When they ease back, walk on. Slowly add busier streets."],t.s)
B.a0z=new A.kE("loose-leash","Loose-leash walking","Your dog walks with you on a loose leash instead of dragging you down the block.",B.abU,B.aaM,!1)
B.aeM=s(["This one can genuinely keep them safe, so make it very worth their while \u2014 pay big.","Trade up: they give up the small thing and get something better.","Practice with boring items long before you need it for real."],t.s)
B.adX=s(["Hold a treat in a closed fist. Let your dog sniff and paw; the moment they stop and back off, mark and treat from the other hand.","Put a treat on the floor and cover it with your hand. Uncover it a little; if they go for it, cover again. Reward when they hold back.",'Add the words "leave it," then practice with harder temptations in more places.'],t.s)
B.a0y=new A.kE("leave-it","Leave it",'Your dog turns away from something tempting when you say "leave it" \u2014 a dropped pill, a chicken bone, a puddle.',B.aeM,B.adX,!1)
B.adq=s([B.a0u,B.a0v,B.a0z,B.a0y],t.mJ)
B.a0q=new A.I2("Manners",B.adq)
B.aaB=s(["Make coming back the best deal around. Pay well for it, especially early on.",'Never call them to something they won\'t like (a bath, leaving the park) \u2014 you don\'t want "come" to start meaning "the fun\'s over."',"Start close and easy; add distance and distraction slowly."],t.s)
B.afn=s(['In a quiet room, say your dog\'s name then "come!" in a bright voice. Reward the moment they reach you.',"Once that's easy, back up a few steps as you call so they trot after you \u2014 reward when they get there.","Take it to the yard, then a long line outside, gradually with more going on around you."],t.s)
B.a0r=new A.kE("recall","Recall","Your dog turns and comes back to you when you call \u2014 even when something more interesting is going on.",B.aaB,B.afn,!1)
B.a94=s(["Build it three ways, one at a time: how long, how far, and how distracting. When you raise one, ease the others.","Return and release before they break it \u2014 set them up to succeed.",'Use a clear release word like "okay" so they know when they\'re free.'],t.s)
B.aaj=s(['Ask for a sit. Wait one second, mark, treat, then say "okay." Slowly stretch the wait.',"Add a small step back, then return and reward. Build the distance a step at a time.","Only once time and distance feel solid, add mild distractions \u2014 and practice in new places."],t.s)
B.a0s=new A.kE("stay","Stay","Your dog holds a sit or a down until you say it's okay to move \u2014 even as you step away.",B.a94,B.aaj,!1)
B.aeN=s(["It's an easy win dogs love \u2014 great for building confidence and refocusing a distracted dog.","Present your hand, mark the nose-bump, then treat.","Keep your hand still and let them come to it."],t.s)
B.ag2=s(["Hold your open palm an inch from their nose. The instant they touch it, mark and treat.","Move your hand a little farther each time so they step over to touch it.",'Add the word "touch," then use it to guide them past distractions or into position.'],t.s)
B.a0A=new A.kE("touch","Hand target (touch)","Your dog boops their nose to your open hand on cue \u2014 a friendly way to move them, redirect them, or say hi.",B.aeN,B.ag2,!1)
B.a9L=s(["Always trade for something as good or better \u2014 dropping should feel like a win, not a loss.","Keep it upbeat; chasing or prying turns it into a game of keep-away.","Practice with legal toys long before you need it for a sock."],t.s)
B.ac0=s(['While your dog holds a toy, offer a treat right at their nose and say "drop it." As they let go, mark and treat.',"Give the toy back afterward \u2014 that teaches that dropping isn't the end of the fun.","Work up to trading for lower-value treats, and practice with different objects in different rooms."],t.s)
B.a0t=new A.kE("drop-it","Drop it","Your dog opens their mouth and lets go of what they're holding when you ask.",B.a9L,B.ac0,!1)
B.ach=s([B.a0r,B.a0s,B.a0A,B.a0t],t.mJ)
